This changes the design of the manifest.json file to have a separate "folders" map for mapping hashed directories. This allows, for example, to add files in a folder like `http_localhost_8000/#testing_5de71/` and have them be resolved automatically as long as their remaining components are identity-mappable to the file system (not hashed). It also saves space in the manifest.json file by only including the hashed directory instead of each descendant file.

```
// manifest.json
{
  "folders": {
    "https://localhost/NOT_MAPPABLE/": "localhost/#not_mappable_5cefgh"
  },
  "modules": {
    "https://localhost/folder/file": {
      "headers": {
        "content-type": "application/javascript"
      }
    },
  }
}

// folder structure
localhost
  - folder
    - #file_2defn (note: I've made up the hashes in these examples)
  - #not_mappable_5cefgh
    - mod.ts
    - etc.ts
    - more_files.ts
```

### Refresh SiteModel when moving back from WebView
To test:
1 - Make sure `JetpackSocialFeatureConfig` feature flag is enabled;
2 - Select a SH site with Jetpack plugin or Jetpack Social plugin installed;
3 - Make sure you have at least one social sharing account connected;
4 - Open post list;
5 - Select a draft or create a new one;
6 - Tap the overflow menu and select "Post settings";
7 - Scroll down to the "Social Sharing" section: the share limit should be shown;
8 - Tap the `SUBSCRIBE TO SHARE MORE` button;
9 - Purchase the plan;
10 - Move back to post settings: the share limit should be gone;

### Fix share limit text color in dark theme
To test:
1 - Make sure `JetpackSocialFeatureConfig` feature flag is enabled;
2 - Select a SH site with Jetpack plugin or Jetpack Social plugin installed;
3 - Make sure you have at least one social sharing account connected;
4 - Open post list;
5 - Select a draft or create a new one;
6 - Tap the overflow menu and select "Post settings";
7 - Scroll down to the "Social Sharing" section;
8 - Observe the share limit description text: it should be visible in light theme and dark theme.

